From 81e41f2246cb0306c2492e2f1c5d4607bad0e79a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:05:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] Cast: Harden route discovery

- Require API 21 for discovery. NsdServiceInfo.getAttributes() does not
  exist before, so resolving a Cast device crashed on API 19 and 20; the
  NewApi lint check was suppressed and is now active again.
- Give up a resolve after 15 s (and stop it on API 34+), so one resolve
  that never completes no longer blocks every later device. Late
  callbacks of a given-up resolve are ignored.
- Resolve a service found several times only once.
- Treat a failed stop of discovery like a stop (NsdManager drops the
  listener either way) and retry a failed start with backoff while
  discovery is wanted.
- Drop disconnected routes that were not found again during a discovery
  run of at least 10 s, so devices that went away while discovery was
  off do not stay published.
- Keep the multizone group bit in the CastDevice capabilities.
